OO-compatible mail backend, development candidate, November 2026.

This is an independent development project. It is not an official ONLYOFFICE
or iRedMail release, and no trademark endorsement is implied.

New Python code, container definitions and configuration in this package are
provided under Apache-2.0; see LICENSE. db/10-schema.sql retains the GPL-3.0-or-later
licence and notices of its iRedMail/PostfixAdmin-derived source. Changes include
the ONLYOFFICE database name, compatibility tables/fields, storage defaults and
InnoDB table engines. See licenses/iRedMail-GPL-3.0.txt.

ONLYOFFICE CommunityServer and Docker-MailServer source was consulted to
identify integration contracts. Pinned source references are in upstream.lock.json.
CommunityServer source and binaries are not included in this package.

Images contain separately licensed Debian, MariaDB, Postfix, Dovecot, Rspamd,
Redis, ClamAV, Python and library packages. Preserve their notices and satisfy
their source-distribution requirements before publishing binary images. The
MariaDB client library is copied with its copyright notice and provenance.
The package is currently a source candidate; binary redistribution has not
received a complete licence review.
